  "content": {
    "id": "p4-q1-group-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "True or False?",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p4-q1-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$3^x\\times5^x=15^x$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}3^x\\times5^x&=(3\\times5)^x\\\\3^x\\times5^x&=15^x\\end{align*}$$True.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q2-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$x^3\\times x^5=x^8$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^3\\times x^5&=x^{3+5}\\\\x^3\\times x^5&=x^8\\end{align*}$$True.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q3-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$3^a\\times5^b=15^{a+b}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "For $a=b=1$, the left side is $3\\times5=15$, but the right side is $15^2=225$. False: the bases are different, so the like-base multiplication law does not apply.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q4-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$a^{\\frac53}=a^5-a^3$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "A fractional index denotes a root: $a^{\\frac53}=\\sqrt[3]{a^5}$. For $a=1$, the printed left side is $1$, while the right side is $1-1=0$. False.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q5-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$x^2(x^3)=x^6$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}x^2(x^3)&=x^{2+3}\\\\x^2(x^3)&=x^5\\end{align*}$$False: multiplication adds the exponents.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q6-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$x^0=0$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False. $x^0=1$ for $x\\ne0$; $0^0$ is undefined.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne0$,$$\\begin{align*}x^0&=x^{1-1}\\\\x^0&=\\frac{x}{x}\\\\x^0&=1.\\end{align*}$$False. At $x=0$, the expression $0^0$ is undefined in this real-algebra context.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q7-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{a^5}{a^3}=a^2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True, for $a\\ne0$.",
          "worked": "For $a\\ne0$,$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{a^5}{a^3}&=a^{5-3}\\\\\\frac{a^5}{a^3}&=a^2.\\end{align*}$$True on the original domain.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q8-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{4^{2x}}{4^2}=4^x$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{4^{2x}}{4^2}&=4^{2x-2}.\\end{align*}$$This equals $4^x$ only when $2x-2=x$, so $x=2$. The statement is not an identity.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q9-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{4^{2x}}{4^x}=4^x$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{4^{2x}}{4^x}&=4^{2x-x}\\\\\\frac{4^{2x}}{4^x}&=4^x.\\end{align*}$$True.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q10-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "j",
        "prompt": "$x^{-2}=-x^2$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne0$, $x^{-2}=\\dfrac1{x^2}$, which is positive, whereas $-x^2$ is negative. False; the original negative power is undefined at $x=0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q11-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "k",
        "prompt": "$x^{\\frac23}=\\sqrt{x^3}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "$x^{\\frac23}=\\sqrt[3]{x^2}$, whereas $\\sqrt{x^3}=x^{\\frac32}$ for $x\\ge0$. For example, at $x=64$ the sides are $16$ and $512$. False; the printed square root requires $x\\ge0$ over the reals.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q12-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "l",
        "prompt": "$(5^x)^2=5^{x^2}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "$(5^x)^2=5^{2x}$. For $x=1$, the printed sides are $25$ and $5$. False: the exponents are multiplied, so $x$ is multiplied by $2$, not squared.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q13-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "m",
        "prompt": "$(5^x)^2=25^x$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "True.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(5^x)^2&=5^{2x}\\\\(5^x)^2&=(5^2)^x\\\\(5^x)^2&=25^x.\\end{align*}$$True.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      },
      {
        "id": "p4-q14-response",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "n",
        "prompt": "$(x^{\\frac13})^2=x^{\\frac26}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "False.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x^{\\frac13})^2&=x^{\\frac13\\times2}\\\\(x^{\\frac13})^2&=x^{\\frac23}.\\end{align*}$$The printed right side is $x^{\\frac13}$ because $\\frac26=\\frac13$. At $x=8$, the sides are $4$ and $2$, so the statement is false.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 6
      }
    ]
  },
